{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We have CNF with 12 variables. Clauses list: \n1. [6,5] meaning x6 ∨ x5\n2. [12,2] x12 ∨ x2\n3. [-4,9] ¬x4 ∨ x9\n4. [-6,1] ¬x6 ∨ x1\n5. [10,4] x10 ∨ x4\n6. [-5,1] ¬x5 ∨ x1\n7. [-7,8] ¬x7 ∨ x8\n8. [-2,11] ¬x2 ∨ x11\n9. [-10,9] ¬x10 ∨ x9\n10. [-12,11] ¬x12 ∨ x11\n11. [-3,8] ¬x3 ∨ x8\n12. [3,7] x3 ∨ x7\n\nWe need count of satisfying assignments of 12 boolean variables.\n\nWe can attempt to analyze constraints. Let's denote variables: x1..x12.\n\nClauses:\n\nC1: x6 ∨ x5\nC2: x12 ∨ x2\nC3: ¬x4 ∨ x9\nC4: ¬x6 ∨ x1\nC5: x10 ∨ x4\nC6: ¬x5 ∨ x1\nC7: ¬x7 ∨ x8\nC8: ¬x2 ∨ x11\nC9: ¬x10 ∨ x9\nC10: ¬x12 ∨ x11\nC11: ¬x3 ∨ x8\nC12: x3 ∨ x7\n\nWe can attempt to find dependencies.\n\nFrom C12: x3 ∨ x7. So at least one of x3, x7 true.\n\nC11: ¬x3 ∨ x8 => if x3 false then x8 true. Equivalent: x3 → x8. Also if x8 false then x3 false? Actually ¬x3 ∨ x8 is equivalent to x3 → x8. So if x3 true, x8 must be true. If x8 false, then x3 must be false.\n\nC7: ¬x7 ∨ x8 => x7 → x8. So both x3 and x7 imply x8. Also if x8 false, then both x3 and x7 false. But we already have at least one of x3,x7 true, so x8 must be true. Because if x8 false, then x3 false and x7 false, contradicting C12. Thus x8 must be true in all satisfying assignments. Good.\n\nThus x8 = 1.\n\nNow C7 satisfied automatically because x8 true. C11 satisfied because x8 true. So x3 and x7 unconstrained except C12: at least one true. So possibilities: (x3=1,x7=0) or (0,1) or (1,1). So 3 possibilities for (x3,x7).\n\nNow consider other clauses.\n\nC1: x6 ∨ x5. So at least one of x6,x5 true.\n\nC4: ¬x6 ∨ x1 => x6 → x1. So if x6 true, x1 must be true. If x6 false, no constraint.\n\nC6: ¬x5 ∨ x1 => x5 → x1. So if x5 true, x1 true.\n\nThus if either x6 or x5 true, x1 must be true. So if at"}}],"created":1790938583,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf",